            <div xml:id="d643">

                <pb facs="0856" n="746" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg746"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.9112A/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Persia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Philip</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-06-25T10:00:00+03:25"><hi rendition="#italic">June 25,
                                1928—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:35
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>65. It is my impression that favorable moment exists now to advance proposal to
                    negotiate treaties of arbitration and conciliation with Persian Government, as
                    mentioned in Department’s telegram No. 39, May 8, 8 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
